+            <t indent="0" pn="section-3.4-17.6.2">These packets are tunnel packets that undergo nested encapsulation.  This node is the entry-point node of both an outer tunnel and one or more of its inner tunnels.</t>
+          </dd>
+        </dl>
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.4-18">The resulting tunnel packets are passed as tunnel  upper-layer output packets through the IPv6 layer (see u.o) down to:</t>
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-3.4-19">(l.o) &quot;tunnel link-layer output&quot; - consists of original IPv6 packets resulting from decapsulation. These packets are passed through the IPv6 layer to:</t>
